item.text:
**Reused evidence**
None materially applicable from the prior chapter dossiers for 5B in 2022.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan's new finance minister faces tight time frame to tackle crises","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-04-20","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/04/20/us-pakistan-politics-financeminister","claim":"Shehbaz Sharif appointed economist and businessman Miftah Ismail as finance minister and tasked him with quickly arresting the economic spiral and restarting IMF talks.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong for contemporaneous appointment and policy context; the Euronews syndication preserves the Reuters text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and at the start of Sharif's tenure.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif's coalition government; the appointment was made by Sharif, though the economic crisis was inherited and IMF constraints remained external.","contrary_evidence":["This appointment alone does not prove later policy quality or implementation."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.7","5B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Statement on Pakistan","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-04-24","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/04/24/pr22131-imf-statement-on-pakistan","claim":"The IMF said prompt action was needed to reverse unfunded subsidies and that Pakistan's authorities requested an EFF extension as a signal of commitment to the program.","locator":"press release text","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF statement issued contemporaneously during Pakistan's program negotiations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target period and immediately after Sharif took office.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-led authorities via the finance minister and cabinet; it reflects program stance under the new government, not solely the prime minister personally.","contrary_evidence":["The statement reflects IMF pressure as much as domestic initiative."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan hikes fuel prices to unlock IMF funding","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-05-26","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/pakistan-hikes-fuel-prices-to-unlock-imf-funding-2830706","claim":"Pakistan raised fuel prices to resume IMF support and reduce fiscal pressure after ending subsidies.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters contemporaneous reporting on a specific policy action with clear fiscal motive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and within Sharif's first months in office.","ruler_attribution":"Implemented by the Sharif coalition through the finance ministry; the decision was ruler-attributable even though IMF conditionality constrained it.","contrary_evidence":["The move was politically costly and worsened near-term inflation for households."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Federal Minister for Finance and Revenue presided over a meeting on PM Relief Package through USC","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-23","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/pr_apr_jun_2022.html","claim":"On the prime minister's directions, the finance minister pursued targeted subsidy proposals to provide immediate relief to lower-income households under a PM relief package.","locator":"June 23, 2022 (PR No. 62)","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government release with direct policy description and named participants.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and while Sharif's cabinet was defining its economic response.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Sharif's directions, though implementation ran through the finance and social safety ministries.","contrary_evidence":["The release is a policy announcement, not proof of successful delivery at scale."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan to raise taxes on rich, ban some car buying to secure IMF bailout","publisher":"Reuters via Euronews","publication_date":"2022-06-11","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/11/pakistan-economy-budget","claim":"The government said it would raise taxes on the rich, ban some government vehicle purchases, and target a 4.9 percent fiscal deficit while seeking IMF bailout support.","locator":"lead paragraph and budget summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters budget reporting on a concrete fiscal package with explicit targets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and the FY2022-23 budget window.","ruler_attribution":"Government policy under Sharif and finance minister Miftah Ismail; the budget was a coalition decision, not a one-man act.","contrary_evidence":["The package was clearly shaped by IMF pressure and austerity needs rather than unconstrained domestic choice."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.7","5B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget Speech 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_Speech_english_2022_23.pdf","claim":"The budget speech said the government chose difficult decisions over political convenience, prioritized economic stability, proposed special taxes on higher incomes, created a task force against tax leakage, and imposed austerity on vehicle and foreign-travel spending.","locator":"pages 2-11, especially lines 41-51 and 180-220","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget speech from the finance ministry with explicit policy commitments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 budget cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Sharif's government and budget team; some wording is rhetorical, but it reflects the government's public policy line.","contrary_evidence":["Speech rhetoric can overstate intent relative to later execution."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.5","5B.7","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Budget in Brief 2022-23","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-10","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/budget/Budget_2022_23/Budget_in_Brief_English.pdf","claim":"The FY2022-23 budget was framed as a sustainable-growth budget built around widening the tax net, reducing the fiscal deficit, protecting vulnerable groups, continuing the IMF programme, targeting subsidies, and increasing taxes on wealthy people.","locator":"Part I, pages 8-9, lines 164-203","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget summary document with concrete policy priorities and fiscal strategy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and the FY2022-23 policy cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Government policy under Sharif's coalition; broader macro conditions and IMF constraints are separate from the ruler's stated priorities.","contrary_evidence":["It is a plan document, so implementation has to be checked elsewhere."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.4","5B.6","5B.7","5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Federal Minister for Finance and Revenue chaired a meeting of Cabinet Committee on Privatisation","publisher":"Ministry of Finance, Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-06-24","url":"https://www.finance.gov.pk/pr_apr_jun_2022.html","claim":"The finance ministry said the CCoP welcomed revival plans for Pakistan Steel Mills through foreign direct investment and technology transfer, and also discussed recapitalizing NPPMCL and private participation in DISCO management to improve viability and service quality.","locator":"June 24, 2022 (PR No. 64)","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official record of a cabinet committee meeting with concrete industrial and utility-sector actions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and under Sharif's government.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif cabinet's economic team; final outcomes depended on later implementation and private-sector response.","contrary_evidence":["The measures are reform proposals and committee decisions, not completed restructuring."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Reaches Staff-Level Agreement on the Combined Seventh and Eighth Reviews for Pakistan's Extended Fund Facility","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-13","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/07/13/pr22255-pakistan-staff-level-agreement-on-7th-and-8th-eff-review","claim":"The IMF said the FY2023 budget aimed for an underlying primary surplus of 0.4 percent of GDP, backed by current-spending restraint, higher-income tax mobilization, protected development spending, and a market-determined exchange rate, while expanding social safety and reforming SOEs.","locator":"press release text and bullet list on policy priorities","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF statement contemporaneous with the policy package and program review.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022, during Sharif's first budget and IMF negotiations.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-led authorities, but shaped by IMF conditionality and provincial bargaining; the central bank retained institutional independence.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF also described FY22 overheating, large deficits, and rising inflation as inherited or policy-induced problems."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Completes the Combined Seventh, and Eighth Reviews of the Extended Fund Facility for Pakistan","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-08-29","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/08/29/pr22293-imf-executive-board-completes-reviews-of-extended-fund-facility-pakistan","claim":"The IMF said Pakistan's authorities had taken important measures to address worsened fiscal and external positions, while the program continued to require a market-determined exchange rate, prudent monetary policy, and structural reforms to improve SOEs and governance.","locator":"press release bullets and paragraphs 241-256","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF review with both retrospective and forward-looking policy assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and after the first phase of Sharif's economic turnaround effort.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif government and its program implementation, but constrained by Ukraine spillovers, inflation, and prior policy choices.","contrary_evidence":["The same IMF review attributed FY22 deficits and reserve erosion to procyclical domestic policies and external shocks."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan picks central bank veteran Jameel Ahmad as new governor","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-19","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/pakistan-names-jameel-ahmad-as-new-central-bank-governor-2876218","claim":"Pakistan appointed career central banker Jameel Ahmad as governor of the State Bank of Pakistan for a five-year term, and he was expected to chair a monetary-policy meeting soon after taking office.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a specific high-level appointment with institutional facts about the appointee.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and relevant to the Sharif government's macro-management decisions.","ruler_attribution":"The governor was appointed by the Sharif government, but the SBP remained an institutionally separate actor.","contrary_evidence":["Appointment quality does not by itself prove the quality of later monetary policy."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Miftah resigns as finance minister to pave way for Dar","publisher":"Dawn","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.dawn.com/news/1712257/miftah-resigns-as-finance-minister-to-pave-way-for-dar","claim":"Miftah Ismail resigned as finance minister, clearing the way for Ishaq Dar to take over after months of internal pressure about key economic decisions, especially fuel prices.","locator":"lead paragraph and resignation note","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting on a specific cabinet turnover and the reasons attached to it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target period and after the first half-year of Sharif's tenure.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Sharif's coalition and party leadership choices; the precise degree of PM autonomy is partly obscured by party-family dynamics.","contrary_evidence":["The resignation also reflects coalition and party politics rather than a clean managerial judgment."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.7","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan swears in Ishaq Dar as finance minister","publisher":"Reuters via The Indian Express","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://indianexpress.com/article/pakistan/pakistan-swears-in-ishaq-dar-as-finance-minister-8177536/","claim":"Ishaq Dar took oath as finance minister while Pakistan was facing a balance-of-payments crisis, foreign reserves near one month of imports, a tumbling rupee, and inflation above 27 percent.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with clear contemporaneous macro facts and a high-level appointment event.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"The appointment was made under Sharif's government, but the macro conditions were inherited and also shaped by global shocks.","contrary_evidence":["The crisis predated Dar's appointment, so the article does not isolate Sharif's own economic competence."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: 2021 Article IV Consultation, Sixth Review Under the Extended Arrangement Under the Extended Fund Facility, and Requests for Waivers...","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-01","url":"https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/002/2022/027/article-A001-en.xml","claim":"The IMF program materials said strengthening governance and control of corruption remained key, including an electronic asset-declaration system and a review of anticorruption institutions such as NAB.","locator":"paragraph 27 in the IMF staff report snippet","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IMF program document with concrete governance benchmarks, though the full article page was blocked for direct open in this environment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The commitment was part of the 2022 IMF program context and remained relevant during Sharif's tenure.","ruler_attribution":"The commitments were made by the Pakistani authorities under the Sharif-led coalition; implementation timing and completeness remained uncertain.","contrary_evidence":["This is a program commitment rather than proof that the anti-corruption reforms were fully implemented in 2022."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan's Economy Slows Down While Inflation Rises Amid Catastrophic Floods","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/06/world-bank-pakistan-s-economy-slows-down-while-inflation-rises-amid-catastrophic-floods","claim":"The World Bank projected only 2 percent growth in FY2023 and said the slowdown reflected flood damage, tight monetary policy, high inflation, and a weaker global environment, with poverty likely to worsen absent decisive relief.","locator":"press release lead paragraphs","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank assessment with explicit macro and poverty projections.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 and directly relevant to end-of-year economic trajectory under Sharif.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly external shocks and inherited macro weakness, but the government's relief and stabilization response still matters for attribution.","contrary_evidence":["This source attributes a large part of the deterioration to floods and external conditions rather than solely to Sharif's choices."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Flood Damages and Economic Losses Over USD 30 billion and Reconstruction Needs Over USD 16 billion - New Assessment","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-28","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/28/pakistan-flood-damages-and-economic-losses-over-usd-30-billion-and-reconstruction-needs-over-usd-16-billion-new-assessme","claim":"The PDNA estimated more than USD 14.9 billion in damages, USD 15.2 billion in losses, and at least USD 16.3 billion in reconstruction needs; it also said the floods affected 33 million people and could push the poverty rate up by several percentage points.","locator":"press release lead paragraphs","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Joint World Bank/ADB/EU/UN assessment using a formal post-disaster methodology.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period and essential for end-state assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Primarily an external shock, but the government's relief and reconstruction choices were directly implicated.","contrary_evidence":["The disaster was not caused by Sharif; it is background for judging response rather than culpability."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Flood Recovery Programme","publisher":"United Nations Development Programme","publication_date":"2022-08","url":"https://www.undp.org/pakistan/frp","claim":"UNDP said the 2022 floods were Pakistan's worst disaster in decades, affecting 33 million people, pushing about 8 million into poverty, and destroying about 2 million houses, while recovery was framed around gender equality and resilience.","locator":"program overview page","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNDP programme page summarizing humanitarian and recovery impacts with clear household-distribution consequences.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and relevant to household-level welfare at the end of Sharif's first year.","ruler_attribution":"This is mostly disaster context, not a direct ruler-policy claim, but it sets the welfare baseline for evaluating response and distribution.","contrary_evidence":["The effects stem from floods, not from an economic policy decision by Sharif."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan's consumer price inflation slows to 23.8%","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-12-01","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/pakistannovembercpi-rises-238-year-on-year-statistics-bureau-2955240","claim":"Pakistan's annual inflation was still 23.8 percent in November after 26.6 percent in October, showing that price pressures remained severe despite policy tightening.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on official inflation data and central-bank reaction.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 and directly relevant to year-end macro management.","ruler_attribution":"The inflation outcome was partly inherited and partly affected by global shocks and floods, but the government's policy response is still attributable.","contrary_evidence":["The month-to-month decline shows some stabilization, so this is mixed rather than pure failure."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across Reuters/Euronews syndications, IMF press releases and country reports, Ministry of Finance budget documents and press releases, World Bank and UNDP flood assessments, and SBP index pages. I retained 16 distinct URLs above and excluded the rest as duplicates, thin syndications of the same Reuters copy, out-of-period material, or context that did not add ruler-attributed economic-choice evidence. I also hit one IMF eLibrary open failure (403) and used the searchable IMF snippet instead. Rejected material included repeated 2023 inflation retrospectives, 2024/2026 IMF pages, generic flood feature stories that duplicated the World Bank/UNDP assessments, and SBP index pages that only listed documents without adding ruler-specific evidence.

**Remaining gaps**
The main gaps are attribution and implementation, not headline macro context. More search would help on:
1. Whether Sharif personally overruled or constrained economic professionals beyond the Miftah-to-Dar turnover.
2. Whether the anti-corruption and asset-declaration commitments were actually implemented in 2022 rather than just promised.
3. Household and regional distribution effects from tax, subsidy, and energy-price changes.
4. Concrete execution of budgeted development spending and the CCoP/privatization decisions.
5. Independent assessments of whether the Dar appointment improved or worsened policy coherence before year-end.
